#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:5
#: fe95a274a94a41c0a5f8ccb82a183116
msgid "Traditional Helicopter – Swashplate Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:7
#: 240bbb0b5e5848229ea04df1c2409198
msgid "The swashplate is designed to take the servo inputs that are based on the pilot’s pitch, roll, and collective commands and translate them to individual blade pitch inputs. There are many different servo arrangements for both three and four servo swashplates. The swashplate library covers all of the popular configurations for both three and four servo swashplates. If you have a unique swashplate, you can also use the generic three servo swashplate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:14
#: 8d24a896a3ba4b678864b12fbbc6e7a4
msgid "Linearize Servo is a feature that you can use for both three and four servo swashplates. However, it is optional for the three servo swashplates as there is no chance for binding. It will most likely always be required for four servo swashplates because of the potential for binding in a four point attachment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:19
#: e5f7a38b38414770a5f661d9afa21823
msgid "The following video covers the swashplate setup and leveling the swashplate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:23
#: bb23ca0f11d64beea98a83bc5ca2f662
msgid "This video covers setting up the min collective, max collective, zero thrust collective, max cyclic and stabilize collective curve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:28
#: 6c66e6da5ca6454eae9c3c444c4b3a89
msgid "Before You Begin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:30
#: f20d0398690540569b4749835b735679
msgid "Prior to beginning the swashplate set up, be sure that your helicopter control linkages are set up in accordance with the assembly instructions. In order to make accurate blade pitch measurements, make the rotor shaft perpendicular to the ground by using shims underneath the landing gear as shown in the picture below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:38
#: e1cd7a4e18834acb88064311e682be1e
msgid "Lastly, it is possible if you haven’t adjusted your tail rotor linkage, or your throttle linkage in the case of a gas engine, you could have binding occur while doing the swashplate set up. This is due to the :ref:`H_SV_MAN <H_SV_MAN>` feature providing manual servo settings that drive the servos to the min and max values. This includes the tail rotor servo and the throttle servo due to throttle curve settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:45
#: 4d5fda919c8e4f36b21066f8a97f3a5f
msgid "Select Swashplate Type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:47
#: d640f2e593ee4dd49e487198266f7ba1
msgid "Below are the swashplate type selections using the :ref:`H_SW_TYPE<H_SW_TYPE__AP_MotorsHeli_Single>` parameter.  The diagrams shown label the servo attach positions as Servo 1, Servo 2 and Servo 3 for the three servo swashplate types.  These also correspond to the default output functions for servo outputs 1 thru 3 on the autopilot for the servos used with these swashplate types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:50
#: 00449ffa059c498892f31a20f539cc18
msgid "For single heli, the servo function assigned to Servo 1 is motor 33, Servo 2 is motor 34, and Servo 3 is motor 35.  These assignments are the same for swashplate 1 for a dual heli frame.  Swashplate 2 for a dual heli defaults to servo outputs 4, 5, and 6 with motors 36, 37 and 38 assigned respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:55
#: e68ed786d41d4cbeb09e3b6ea25fac2a
msgid "For four servo swashplates, the fourth servo (Servo 5) on the single heli frame defaults to servo output 5 and is assigned motor 37. For the dual heli frame, the fourth servo (Servo 7) on swashplate 1 defaults to servo output 7 and is assigned motor 39. The fourth servo (Servo 8) on swashplate 2 defaults to servo output 8 and is assigned motor 40 function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:59
#: 6ef3b0eb838c4591a798d9cefa135f87
msgid "In the case of dual heli frame with four servo swashplates, the RSCHeli output function (Motor 31) will need to be assigned to another servo output than its normal default of servo output 8."
msgstr ""

